# PC card pc-melee-end (docs/bench/melee-top3.md, HAND-4 and HAND-5, BENCH-171): one build alone on today's whole melee field, 46 fields x 6 fresh seeds (3265-3270, after pc-melee-hand's 3259-3264), at the machine's melee width (@C@, fixed at prep) and CPU constant; the bench drops the robots broken-1.11.2.txt lists (BENCH-169). Template: meprep writes work/melee-end-<arm>.args with @V@ = the robot.release in hadur-robot/pom.xml and @A@ = the arm's suffix (aa, bb, eg, ek); every arm fights the same fields and seeds, so the read pairs them battle for battle.
--suite
melee-census-317.txt
--seeds
6
--seed-base
3264
--rounds
35
--parallel
@C@
--child-heap
2G
--cpu-constant
auto
--robot-jar
bisect/hadur117.Hadur_@V@@A@.jar
--robot
hadur117.Hadur @V@@A@
--out
work/melee-end-@V@-@A@
--report
../docs/bench/local/melee-end-@A@.md
